{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/113028","id":3035170334,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc606QYe","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113028","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113028.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113028.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113028","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/113028/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/113028/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113028/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/3fee7c24647baca7daa962d07cc28a8b4392a2ce","number":113028,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Fix assertions against buffer overruns in `input_event_codec.cpp`","user":{"login":"madsbangh","id":2969321,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5NjkzMjE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2969321?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/madsbangh","html_url":"https://github.com/madsbangh","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/madsbangh/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/madsbangh/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/madsbangh/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/madsbangh/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/madsbangh/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/madsbangh/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/madsbangh/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/madsbangh/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/madsbangh/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I noticed `DisplayServerEmbeddedState::serialize` (in platform/macos/display_server_embedded.mm) had its assertion at the end fixed by @stuartcarnie from\r\n`DEV_ASSERT((data - r_data.ptrw()) >= r_data.size());`\r\nto\r\n`DEV_ASSERT(r_data.size() >= (data - r_data.ptrw()));`\r\nin commit c62ad8dc655c410b28bc80bce251d0e0f7e170ad\r\n\r\nThis makes sense, but I wanted to compare this change to similar asserts elsewhere.\r\nEventually this lead me to core/input/input_event_codec.cpp, which has a handful of equivalent assertions, also by @stuartcarnie.\r\n\r\nIt makes sense because we want to assert the buffer we are reading from / writing to is *at least as long* as the amount we have moved our `data`pointer while decoding/encoding.\r\n\r\nThis PR just follows his example and applies that fix to the `DEV_ASSERT`s in input_event_codec.cpp as well.","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":890310664,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw4OTAzMTA2NjQ=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:input","name":"topic:input","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":12939969,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AxXLB","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/23","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/23","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/23/labels","number":23,"state":"closed","title":"4.6","description":"","creator":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_ur